  "id": "DrugBank_DB11952 - MONDO_3864",
  "verbalization": "Duvelisib, through its indication for Richter Syndrome and Acute Lymphoblastic/lymphocytic Leukemia, shares a common pathway with Idelalisib, which is known to target Chronic Lymphocytic Leukemia/small Lymphocytic Lymphoma. The evidence suggests that Duvelisib may exert its therapeutic effect on this leukemia subset through a mechanism of action similar to Idelalisib, possibly by inhibiting phosphatidylinositol 3-kinase (PI3K) signaling, a key pathway in many leukemias. The high scores in both paths indicate a strong association between Duvelisib and the target condition, suggesting a potential role in the treatment of Chronic Lymphocytic Leukemia/small Lymphocytic Lymphoma. The overlapping indications and the shared mechanism of action support the integration of these findings, highlighting a possible link between Duvelisib and this leukemia type through a common therapeutic target.",
